      ]
    }
  ],
  "accuracyFacts": [
    "IEnumerable<T> and IQueryable<T> describe sequence/query abstractions; neither implies the source is necessarily in-memory or remote. IQueryable behavior is defined by its provider, which may translate only supported expression-tree shapes.",
    "AsEnumerable changes the compile-time operator binding for subsequent calls; it does not itself enumerate, materialize, or execute the source. Enumeration later can still invoke an underlying IQueryable provider for the preceding query.",
    "AsQueryable over an ordinary in-memory sequence may wrap it with an in-memory provider; it does not automatically create remote translation.",
    "Queryable does not provide every Enumerable terminal/materialization method. Enumerable.ToLookup and Enumerable.ToList can consume an IQueryable through IEnumerable and then execute via enumeration; they are not Queryable operators.",
    "LINQ deferred operators usually execute on enumeration, but some operators execute immediately and return a scalar or materialized collection. Distinct is deferred and can yield unique items incrementally while retaining a set of seen values; it is not an all-input buffering operator.",
    "OrderBy is deferred but non-streaming for LINQ to Objects: it consumes and sorts the input before yielding the first ordered result. GroupBy for LINQ to Objects also builds groups before yielding. Provider-backed behavior is provider-specific.",
    "IAsyncEnumerable<T> denotes asynchronous enumeration, not necessarily network I/O or parallel processing. .NET 10 introduced the platform AsyncEnumerable class; use System.Linq.AsyncEnumerable for earlier targets and verify package versions for individual additions such as FullJoin. AsyncEnumerable.ToListAsync returns ValueTask<List<T>>, not Task<List<T>>; several async sequence terminal operators use ValueTask results.",
    "Repeated enumeration of a deferred query repeats its work; for a provider-backed IQueryable, this can reissue a provider query. Whether it causes a database round trip depends on the provider and source.",
    "Filter or project remotely only when the actual provider supports translation; do not imply every IQueryable source is a database query or that unsupported expressions are always silently evaluated client-side."
  ],
